# A push that changes this file on the working branch starts .github/workflows/ctqw-hardware.yml, which acts on the
# LAST LINE of this file and on nothing else. The last line must be exactly one of:
#   none                 nothing runs
#   check                read-only access check (submits nothing)
#   dryrun               one server-side dry run (validated by the service, mock results, no device executes)
#   submit N             submit repetition N (1 to 5), first attempt, to a real device
#   submit N attempt A   resubmit repetition N after a rejection before execution (A from 2 to 9)
#   collect N            fetch the job of repetition N (submits nothing)
# Anything else, including a trailing space, makes the workflow stop without doing anything.
# Every action except "none" needs the owner's release of the job in the GitHub environment "ibm-hardware", which
# is where the credentials live. The lead writes a line here only on the owner's explicit instruction for that line.
none
